  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_2689964bd1204431a7eced96edbe9587",
      "statement": "Gait phase is not stored in any generated database and is reconstructed from the foot contacts: pi per footfall, linear between footfalls, and per clip so no stride is interpolated across a boundary. A clip with fewer than two footfalls is reported as having no measurable cycle rather than being given a fabricated one, which a zero phase rate marks.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/gait_phase.py#L1-L40",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0ee0919becfecc05c058281bc776fd5ab228b7de9148b9561e14e8aa1586c5e6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/gait_phase.py#L94-L168",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0a293cd6b71831e024916cd131ccc25836e30f1714179e5f39ab8d86c53c5b13:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/tests/test_gait_phase.py",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:6011487f104b0a1f68ba9747aa212bbe77e5576d22c8dacb20f3d448226c6eaf"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_202fd6cda1724895b476a9da4b7e0425",
      "statement": "training_data deliberately builds neither network's input tensor, only the per-frame quantities underneath both, because the packing is a property of the model rather than of the database; the PFNN packing therefore lives in pfnn_dataset rather than in training_data.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/training_data.py#L1-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:302df164afe03076d6ab54f04c8cc431a17834b91da24778fa898e411470e895:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/pfnn_dataset.py#L1-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fc9c20e8eb29e505fb21b7a462acea31da4d6f611da13e6fb6b30b36e24a8754:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7d8a3afbdff84c8dadb734032cb18e04",
      "statement": "The character-frame conversion has one named definition per side — training_data.build_training_set for training and CharacterSpacePose.Extract for inference — because a disagreement between them about frame, units or rate convention does not throw and shows up only as bad motion.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/CharacterSpacePose.cs#L7-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a100a836ceb11acf80a86ca3d5df039cb278478bf48ec7939cb730fa033ac10:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/training_data.py#L361-L458",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:89297db0d4ea26ba80d8e528a71f2e480f6fd7c9181c70e6e3f1a8dcea2d7419:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3f6f7075d1ec4b65beb7a0ed74219c08",
      "statement": "The two sides' rates are not identical by construction: Python differences consecutive frame-local poses of a stored database while the C# composes the instantaneous rate implied by a pose's own velocity channels, and since those channels are themselves finite differences over the same timestep the two agree to first order and exactly for motion rigid within the frame.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Pose/CharacterSpacePose.cs#L7-L30",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7a100a836ceb11acf80a86ca3d5df039cb278478bf48ec7939cb730fa033ac10:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/training_data.py#L340-L360",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:74861af2650c5dfd61142afd4ee2c5c1e78461112a8f5dd4f272377dc065aefe:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_41b36fb16ea4465f9b7015ef7410f645",
      "statement": "A trajectory window is the one model input the frame-local arrays cannot supply, because the frame transform is precisely what removes it, so the training set keeps the world frame origin and heading for that purpose alone and TrainingSet.trajectory_window derives the window from them at whatever offsets a model wants.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/training_data.py#L121-L175",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f8c066c0f54cf0abc8901031810709c36897e0f43d1e7d621e163b182855b49:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/training_data.py#L248-L299",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70a05aa0f04ec2de81d8a4c81396a1e2e76a00259ce229d52a11b6ff369ed722:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_533dffb43e484223bf3e0e1da9e0cb93",
      "statement": "Trajectory window offsets are clamped inside the query frame's own clip rather than wrapped or dropped, so a window near a clip edge repeats its last real sample — the same thing a character standing still would produce — which keeps every frame usable instead of discarding the ends of every clip.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Python/training_data.py#L248-L299",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:70a05aa0f04ec2de81d8a4c81396a1e2e76a00259ce229d52a11b6ff369ed722:"
        },
        {
